**Fix sortedCopy(nums)**

`sortedCopy` must not change its input, so its parameter is `readonly number[]` — and now it doesn't compile, because `sort` sorts in place. Fix it.

```ts
function sortedCopy(nums: readonly number[]): number[] {
  return nums.sort((a, b) => a - b);
}
```

notes.back:
// Why: A readonly array type has no mutating methods (push, sort, splice…), so the
// compiler catches the accidental mutation. Copy first, or use toSorted().
// Docs: https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/2/objects.html
function sortedCopy(nums: readonly number[]): number[] {
  return [...nums].sort((a, b) => a - b);
}

